1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,422
Mezo gives anyone a Bitcoin-backed loan.

2
00:00:03,371 --> 00:00:09,061
Pylon makes that loan something you can steer: leverage it, deleverage
it, or defend it.

3
00:00:09,061 --> 00:00:11,458
One transaction each.

4
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:20,496
Every Mezo trove sits in one redemption queue: four hundred and
twenty-nine million MUSD deep, across two hundred and ninety-six

5
00:00:20,445 --> 00:00:26,917
Redemptions start at the lowest ratio above one hundred and ten
percent, with no liquidation warning.

6
00:00:26,917 --> 00:00:30,862
Repaying needs MUSD a borrower may not have.

7
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,591
Paste any trove.

8
00:00:33,541 --> 00:00:43,332
Pylon reads it live: zero point zero four five seven BTC against two
thousand and fifty-one MUSD of debt, at one hundred and eighty-one

9
00:00:43,332 --> 00:00:46,158
No migration, no custody.

10
00:00:46,158 --> 00:00:50,103
The owner authorises every action with one signature.

11
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:59,446
A flash loop borrows MUSD, swaps it to BTC, posts that BTC as
collateral, and repays the flash loan in the same transaction.

12
00:00:59,396 --> 00:01:08,080
Pylon sizes it against the one hundred and fifty percent collateral
floor, then prices every leg and the exact debt delta the signature

13
00:01:09,079 --> 00:01:18,990
The shield reserve is the other half: one thousand one hundred and
seven MUSD of pooled capital, lent only to a registered position, and

14
00:01:18,939 --> 00:01:22,990
The claim blocks collateral release until the loan is settled.

15
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:25,545
And it has run.

16
00:01:25,495 --> 00:01:38,138
Fourteen explorer-linked transactions: reserve deposits, loops, an
unwind, a full exit, and an autonomous keeper that defended a shielded

17
00:01:38,138 --> 00:01:43,503
The audited generation is live on mainnet too, funded with real MUSD.

18
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:45,690
Pylon.

19
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:49,690
Non-custodial leverage and defence for Mezo troves.

20
00:01:49,690 --> 00:01:56,695
Forty-three contract tests, a twelve-lens security review, a live
terminal, and a public repository.

